{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-724d9d9153234f61a160","statement":"Let $\\bA$ be a complete local algebra over\nalgebraically closed field $\\Mk$. Then $\\bA $ is derived tame if\nand only if $\\bA$ is isomorphic to one of the following algebras:\n\n- $\\bL_1= \\Mk.$\n\n- The algebra of dual numbers $\\bL_2=\\Mk[x]/(x^{2}).$\n\n- The power series algebra $\\bL_3=\\Mk [[x]].$\n\n- $\\bL_4=\\Mk [[x,y]]/(xy)$ - the local ring of a simple node of an algebraic curve over a field $\\Mk$.\n\n- The dihedral algebra $\\bL_5=\\Mk \\left<\\left< x,y\\right>\\right> /(x^{2}, y^{2})$.\n\nMoreover, the first algebra is derived finite and the second and\nthird are derived discrete.","source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"6b649c4b442544cd14ed1b47e86e3ffc8703f08541feefbbfaa207e2e8114a90","kind":"result","label":"Result 1","ref_key":"","name":"","order":1,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"4691b7e6310aff594015f4ee9295f0c5d77eb87af5ba0a297bb3f4cdbb2ee258","line":163,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:07+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":574,"math_hints":47}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","title":"Derived tame local and two-point algebras","abstract":"We determine derived representation type of complete finitely generated local and two-point algebras over an algebraically closed field.","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Yuriy Drozd","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2008","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"lenght":"\\mathop\\mathrm{lenght}\\nolimits","md":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{mod}","pr":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{pro}","bp":"\\bullet","iso":"\\simeq","iff":"if and only if","setsuch":"\\left\\{\\,#1\\,|\\,#2\\,\\right\\}","rad":"\\mathop\